      "claim": "Refusing entry to a place open to the public solely because of origin, skin colour or religion (e.g. a pub sign barring guests from ex-Yugoslavia/Albania) is an unlawful personality infringement (Art. 28 Civil Code) and breaches Art. 261bis Criminal Code (up to 3 years or a monetary penalty).",
